There is a logic bug in the de-duplication key generation. Since `target.name` is equal to the environment variable name (which is unique for each item in `names`), the key `${target.name}:${target.redacted_url}` will always be unique. This prevents the `seen` Set from filtering out duplicate URLs configured across different environment variables (e.g., `SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` pointing to the same host). Use `target.redacted_url` as the de-duplication key instead.

